<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000094> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In ball culture, ballroom families (or houses) are chosen families headed by and named after established community members (e.g., the House of Xtravaganza); heads of ballroom families are typically called \"mothers\" or \"fathers,\" while members are termed \"children\" and \"siblings.\"" .
