<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000949> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The most important gay and lesbian sporting event in Europe, hosted by license of the European Gay and Lesbian Sport Federation (EGLSF)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000949> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An international sport and cultural event held by the Federation of Gay Games since 1982 that promotes acceptance of LGBTQ+ people and features LGBTQ+ athletes, artists, and other individuals" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000949> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Organized games or sports activities for LGBTQ+ people or communities; includes both competitive and recreational events." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000949> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A sporting and cultural event open to anyone regardless of sexual identity or qualifying standards that is intended to bring together athletes and artists from around the globe, many from countries where homosexuality remains illegal; separate from the Gay Games" .
