<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000436> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "FtM transsexuals" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000436> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "F2Ms" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000436> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Transsexual men" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000436> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Female-to-male" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000436> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "FtM (female-to-male) is a mostly historical term which has been largely replaced by “trans men.” This is due in part to the term's role in the medicalization of transgender people and the assumption that trans men were previously “female” and have become “male” (typically through hormones and/or surgery)." .
