<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000898> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Term used by the Māori people, or people who are part of the Indigenous Polynesian people of mainland Aotearoa (New Zealand), that was historically used to describe an \"intimate companion of the same sex.\" In the 1980s, the term was reclaimed for use by lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender, queer, intersex people, and other members of Rainbow communities. Only use to refer to individuals who identify as Takatāpui." .
