<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002847> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002847> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002847> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002847> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 3.7.1" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002848> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002848" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002848> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Isolated 17,20-lyase deficiency" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002848> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "ILD" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002848> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "People with isolated 17,20-lyase deficiency (ILD) have one of several specific variations in their genes that cause their bodies to make lower-than-typical amounts of testosterone. They may be born with genitals that do not appear quite like a typical penis, and their testes may be descended or undescended. In adolescence, they may not experience all of the changes related to a typical testosterone puberty because their variation impacts their hormone production." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002848> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000669> .
